1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

  (a) Read the source code.

  (b) Build the mod from the source code and run it yourself, changed or not, for
      your own personal use.

  (c) Prepare changes to offer back to this project through its repository.

  (d) Use the mod as released by the author on your own computer and show it in
      videos, streams and screenshots.

  (e) Point to the author's own download pages on CurseForge and Modrinth, for
      example from a modpack that fetches the mod from those pages. That is not
      redistribution, as long as the file itself is not copied into the pack.


2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO WITHOUT WRITTEN PERMISSION

  (a) Publish, upload, sell or otherwise redistribute the mod or its source code,
      changed or not, on CurseForge, Modrinth or anywhere else.

  (b) Publish a project made from this one, or a part of it, under any name.

  (c) Use the name Mosaicary or its icon for another project.


